etimes there's real value to  be gained from simply thinking something  might be true rather than whether it's  actually true and that's why I dropped  this idea into the video let's finish by  talking about the dragons the ancient  dragon is worth talking about because  for whatever reason he has direct links  to sin the slumbering dragon of the DLC  the gigantic dragon has the soul of a  giant not the soul of an ancient dragon  he also resides in Althea's keep a place  where experimentation is a key theme in  the Eyrie we find links to sin that make  me think that sin came before the  ancient dragon so deep within we find a  petrified egg the description of which  states eggs are vessels that harbor life  itself and symbolize the deepest secrets  of existence but what does a petrified  egg harbor behind the egg is a mural  depicting an ancient civilization and  the dragon they worshiped this is a  mural also found deep within the sunken  city and it represents sin the  slumbering dragon if you take this  speculation as far as it goes you could  surmise that vendrick stole an egg from  the sleeping dragon and used it to help  him create his own dragon  you could also surmise that maybe the  mural didn't have its origin in the  depths and that maybe it's found  everywhere because it's really popular  I'm a bit stumped on this one so let me  know what do you think that's it though  to reiterate you should check out this  video if you haven't already I'm pretty  happy with it there's a great story to  be told in the sunken city so feel free  to rate the video let me know what you  thought follow me on patreon - I'll see  you later
 

